le osteoporosis model via IGF-I and the RANK pathway</article-title><source>Bone</source><year>2006</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>1331</fpage><lpage>1342</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16890505</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ijms-10-00292"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cho</surname><given-names>M-H</given-names></name><name><surname>Paik</surname><given-names>Y-S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hahn</surname><given-names>T-R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Enzymatic conversion of precarthamin to carthamin by a purified enzyme from the yellow petals of safflower</article-title><source>J. Agric. Food Chem</source><year>2000</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>3971</fpage><lpage>3921</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b17-ijms-10-00292"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name></person-group><source>Castor, sesame and safflower</source><publisher-name>Barnes and Noble, Inc</publisher-name><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><year>1971</year><fpage>529</fpage><lpage>744</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b18-ijms-10-00292"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical application of safflower (<italic>Carthamus tinctorius</italic>) [in Chinese]</article-title><source>Zhejiang J. Trad. Chinese Med</source><year>1985</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>42</fpage><lpage>43</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b19-ijms-10-00292"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Yi Qi Huo Xue Prescription used for treatment o